Error [E2417]: explicit failure domain `String (text)` is not an Error type
  --> tests/ui/fallible_arm_table_tail.jet:1:12
    |
  1 | fn maybe() Int !String -> .Ok(1)
    |            ^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A `!` contract may name `Err`, a Core error, a type marked `#Error`, an all-error union, or `Never`; arbitrary value types do not describe failures.
 Fix: use a Core error, add `#Error` to a local error type, or remove the explicit error contract.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2417

Error [E0330]: can't infer the enum type for `.Ok`
  --> tests/ui/fallible_arm_table_tail.jet:1:27
    |
  1 | fn maybe() Int !String -> .Ok(1)
    |                           ^^^^^^
 Why: a leading-dot variant needs a known enum type from context
 Fix: add a type annotation, or write the full form `EnumName.Ok`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0330

Error [E0307]: this `if` over `Int (a whole number)` has no `else` arm — range arms can't cover every value
  --> tests/ui/fallible_arm_table_tail.jet:5:5
    |
  5 |     if result == {
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `Int (a whole number)` has infinitely many values; range arms only cover a subset
 Fix: add `else -> { … }` to handle values not matched by any range
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0307

Error [E0305]: pattern `Ok` doesn't match Int (a whole number)
  --> tests/ui/fallible_arm_table_tail.jet:6:9
    |
  6 |         .Ok(_) -> { print(true) }
    |         ^^^^^^
 Why: variant patterns only work on enum values
 Fix: test an enum value, or use `Val` / `None` for optionals
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0305

Error [E0116]: `print` doesn't hand back a value
  --> tests/ui/fallible_arm_table_tail.jet:6:21
    |
  6 |         .Ok(_) -> { print(true) }
    |                     ^^^^^
 Why: a call is a value only when its function declares a result after the parameter list
 Fix: inside an arm, wrap the call in `{ … }`; otherwise put `print` on its own line, or declare it as `fn print(…) Type -> …`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0116

Error [E0305]: pattern `Err` doesn't match Int (a whole number)
  --> tests/ui/fallible_arm_table_tail.jet:7:9
    |
  7 |         .Err(_) -> { print(false) }
    |         ^^^^^^^
 Why: variant patterns only work on enum values
 Fix: test an enum value, or use `Val` / `None` for optionals
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0305

Error [E0116]: `print` doesn't hand back a value
